<%#
  Context menu component - what a right click on an item offers

  The element it is rendered in says `data-context-menu`; context_menu_controller.js
  (on <body>) shows this menu at the pointer on a right click, a long press, Shift+F10
  or the menu key. Fill it with components/menu_item and components/menu_divider.
  Nothing in it runs until it is shown: it is a <template>.

  Required:
    label: What the menu is about, for a screen reader ("Conversation", "Card")

  Example (in the item's view):
    tag.div data: { context_menu: true } do
      ...
      render "components/context_menu", label: "Card" do
        render "components/menu_item", text: "Archive", icon: "archive", href: path, method: :post
      end
    end
%>
<%= tag.template data: { context_menu_items: true }, aria: { label: label } do %>
  <%= yield %>
<% end %>
